  "rows": [
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:1537",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    The weekly window values of one weekday must not overlap. Adjacent windows are\n    allowed and merge.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:1644",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    A weekly window must start and end on the 30-minute grid, and an off-grid time\n    is rejected.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:1745",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    The open time must be computed per concrete local date and then converted to\n    instants, never precomputed in UTC.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:1867",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Only the room owner may add or remove a weekly window or blackout, and each\n    edit must run inside the transaction that Booking opens under the room lock and\n    passes to the transactional entry of Availability, which only Booking may\n    import and which never opens the lock itself.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2160",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    An edit to a weekly window or blackout must not sweep, decline, or cancel any\n    booking. The sweep that follows an edit belongs to Booking, in the same\n    transaction.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2336",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability depends on Rooms for the room timezone and room owner,\n    and on SharedKernel for the conversion of a local span.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2483",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Weekly window values on Monday from 09:00 to 12:00 and from 11:00 to 15:00 are\n    rejected as overlapping, while 09:00 to 12:00 and 12:00 to 15:00 are accepted\n    and merge in the open time.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2681",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    A weekly window starting at 09:15 is rejected as off the 30-minute grid.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2759",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Adding a blackout for a date removes that date's open time and leaves the next\n    date unaffected, and removing the blackout restores the open time.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:291",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "goal",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Let a room owner say when a room is open, and let other modules ask for that\n    open time over a date range.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:2914",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Given weekly window values on Friday from 18:00 to 24:00 and on Saturday from\n    00:00 to 02:00, the open time is one continuous span from Friday 18:00 to\n    Saturday 02:00.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3095",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    A signed-in user who is not the room owner cannot add or remove a weekly window\n    or blackout.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3197",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    A blackout on a past date is accepted and changes no open time that can still\n    matter.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3310",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability provides the edit of a weekly window and a blackout through its\n    own transactional entry, for Booking's editing workflow to use.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3460",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability provides the open time of a room over a local date range as\n    UTC instant ranges, to Booking and Calendar.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3587",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability provides the blackout dates of a room, for Calendar to show to the\n    room owner.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3688",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability provides the current weekly window and blackout entries of a room\n    to its room owner, so the manage page can show them.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:3847",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Weekly windows plus whole-day blackouts were chosen over weekly-only hours and\n    over date overrides that can also open time, because they give enough\n    expressiveness with one precedence rule.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:4050",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Adjacent weekly windows merge instead of being rejected, since only a true\n    overlap is ambiguous.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:420",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability owns each *weekly window* of a room, which is a weekday with a\n    local start and end on the 30-minute grid in the room timezone. The end may be\n    24:00, and a weekday may have any number of them.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:638",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Availability owns each *blackout*, which covers one whole room-local date of a\n    room.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:732",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    The *open time* of a room is its weekly window values minus its blackout dates,\n    expressed as UTC instant ranges.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:availability.sigil:868",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:availability.sigil:Availability",
      "componentLabel": "Availability",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "availability.sigil",
      "prose": "    Computing open time for a room over a local date range takes five steps. Step\n    one reads the room timezone and the weekly window values of the room. Step two\n    collects, for each concrete local date in the range, the weekly window values\n    of its weekday as local span values. Step three drops every date that has a\n    blackout. Step four hands the local span values to SharedKernel, which converts\n    them to UTC instant ranges, drops slots inside a daylight-saving gap, and\n    merges adjacent ranges, including 24:00 joining 00:00 of the next day. Step\n    five returns the merged UTC instant ranges as the open time to the caller.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1029",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Module commands and queries must not read the session themselves. They take the\n    signed-in user as an explicit actor.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1155",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    A user account must not carry a role. Owning and renting come from a user's\n    relationship to rooms and requests.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1290",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Signing up and then signing in creates a session, and resolving the\n    signed-in user from that session's headers returns the user.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1428",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Resolving the signed-in user with no session or an invalid one returns no user,\n    and requireUser then refuses as unauthenticated.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1566",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Submitting a form after clearing the session changes nothing and is refused.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1648",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Signing out ends the session, and the next page load redirects to sign-in.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1746",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity lets a person sign up, sign in, and sign out with email and password\n    on a user account.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1852",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity provides requireUser, which returns the signed-in user for the current\n    session or refuses as unauthenticated. Every page and action except sign-up and\n    sign-in calls it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:195",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity owns each *user account*, which has one email and one password\n    credential and no stored role.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2043",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity provides resolution of the session from request headers outside\n    Next.js, so the signed-in user can be tested without a running app.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2211",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Better Auth backs Identity because Auth.js is security-fixes-only and Lucia is\n    deprecated.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2311",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Roles come from the relationship, not the account, so one person can own and\n    rent without two accounts.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:30",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "goal",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Establish who is acting on every page and action, with one account type and\n    email and password sign-in, so the rest of Slotted never guesses.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:307",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity owns each *session* created at sign-in and ended at sign-out.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:397",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Resolving the *signed-in user* takes four steps. Step one reads the session\n    from the request headers. Step two looks up the user account that the session\n    belongs to. Step three returns the signed-in user, or returns no user when the\n    session is missing or invalid. Step four turns a missing user into an\n    unauthenticated refusal at the requireUser gate, and otherwise hands the\n    signed-in user to the calling page or action.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:864",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    The optimistic redirect on the session cookie is not a security boundary. Only\n    requireUser may decide whether a signed-in user exists for a page or action.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:1248",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Only the room owner may edit a room, archive it, unarchive it, or change its\n    room timezone.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:1349",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Every room-scoped mutation, including availability edits and booking status\n    changes made by other modules, must run inside the room lock. Changes to\n    different rooms must not block each other.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:1554",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms exposes a *transactional entry*, a second entry beside the module public\n    entry that runs inside the room lock and that only Booking may import. Rooms\n    must expose the archive, unarchive, and room timezone mutations only through\n    its transactional entry, and Rooms must not import Booking.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:1864",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms depends on Identity and requires the signed-in user to record a\n    room owner.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:1969",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Creating a room with an invalid room timezone is rejected.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2033",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Editing a room by a signed-in user who is not its room owner is refused.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2111",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    The room list excludes every archived room and includes rooms from every\n    room owner.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2205",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Unarchiving an archived room returns it to the room list.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2268",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Two concurrent changes under the room lock on one room run one after the other,\n    while changes on different rooms do not block each other.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2433",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms lets a signed-in user create a room, and lets the room owner edit its\n    name, description, capacity, and location text.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:250",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms owns each *room*, which has a name, description, capacity, location text,\n    and a *room timezone* that is an IANA zone required at creation. Capacity is\n    informational and a request carries no party size.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2566",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides the *room list* of every room that is not an archived room to\n    any signed-in user.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2672",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides archive, unarchive, and room timezone change of a room through\n    its transactional entry, for Booking's workflows to use.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2816",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides the room lock, which opens a transaction on one room and hands\n    it to a change, for Booking's workflows and the commands of Rooms to use.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:2977",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides the room owner of a room so other modules can authorize a\n    signed-in user against it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:3086",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides the room timezone of a room so other modules can read a range in\n    it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:3179",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Rooms provides each room owner the list of every room that owner created,\n    including each archived room, so the owner can reach an archived room to\n    unarchive it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:3371",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    The room timezone is locked while upcoming items exist because no booking\n    should ever move in time. That check lives in Booking, which is why Rooms never\n    imports it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:3550",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    A row lock in Postgres serializes room changes because the no-overlap rule and\n    exact automatic declines need one ordering per room.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:471",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Every room has exactly one *room owner*, the signed-in user who created it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:552",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    A room is either listed or an *archived room*. Rooms owns the archived room\n    mark: a room carries it from archive until unarchive.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:705",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Creating a room takes three steps. Step one requires a signed-in user. Step two\n    validates the room timezone against the IANA zone list and rejects an unknown\n    zone. Step three records the signed-in user as the room owner and returns the\n    new room.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:84",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "goal",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Let any signed-in user list a room for others to rent, keep the set of rooms\n    browsable, and give every room-scoped change one serialized path.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:rooms.sigil:968",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:rooms.sigil:Rooms",
      "componentLabel": "Rooms",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "rooms.sigil",
      "prose": "    Running a change under the *room lock* takes three steps. Step one opens a\n    transaction and locks the row of the room. Step two passes the transaction to\n    the change. Step three commits and returns the result, or rolls back if the\n    change fails.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1121",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    Every check against the current time must read the *clock* and never the\n    database now(), so tests can create an item before its start and act after it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1282",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    A half-open range includes its start and excludes its end, so two ranges that\n    meet at one instant do not overlap.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1405",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    A boundary must lie on the 30-minute grid, and 24:00 is allowed only as the end\n    of a local span.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1525",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    A local time of 09:00 or 09:30 is on the 30-minute grid, and 09:15 is rejected.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1610",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    The half-open range 09:00 to 10:00 and the half-open range 10:00 to 11:00 do\n    not overlap, while 09:00 to 10:30 and 10:00 to 11:00 do.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1753",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    In America/New_York, 02:00 on the spring-forward date is a\n    nonexistent local time, and 01:30 on the fall-back date is an\n    ambiguous local time that resolves to the earlier UTC instant.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:1950",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    A local span from 01:00 to 04:00 on the spring-forward date in America/New_York\n    yields two real hours of UTC instant ranges.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2084",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    In Asia/Kolkata a local span still aligns to the 30-minute grid in local time\n    even though local :00 is UTC :30, and Australia/Lord_Howe's 30-minute\n    daylight-saving shift yields correct spans.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2307",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    SharedKernel provides the clock to every command and query. Server actions pass\n    the system clock, and tests pass a fixed one.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2442",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    SharedKernel provides the checks on the 30-minute grid and the resolution of a\n    nonexistent local time or ambiguous local time to a UTC instant.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:245",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    Resolving a requested boundary in a zone takes three steps. Step one checks\n    that the local time is on the *30-minute grid*. Step two rejects a\n    *nonexistent local time*. Step three resolves an *ambiguous local time* to its\n    earlier occurrence and returns the resulting *UTC instant* to the caller.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2595",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    SharedKernel provides the conversion of a local span to merged half-open range\n    values of UTC instant.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2706",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    SharedKernel provides a *domain error* for each expected failure, such as a\n    lost race or a rejected boundary, so callers map it to a user message without\n    exposing internals.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:2911",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    Time uses Temporal through temporal-polyfill because daylight-saving arithmetic\n    is central to the domain, and moving to native Temporal waits for a runtime\n    that ships it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:3095",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    The 30-minute grid and half-open ranges were chosen over any-minute ranges and\n    whole-day bookings to keep the calendar tidy and back-to-back bookings\n    conflict-free.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:34",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "goal",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    Give every module one agreed way to measure and compare time, so that a booking\n    ending at 10:00 never conflicts with one starting at 10:00 and no module holds\n    a different idea of now.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:558",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    Converting a *local span* to instants takes two steps. Step one turns each\n    30-minute slot of the span into a UTC instant range and drops every slot inside\n    a daylight-saving gap. Step two merges adjacent ranges, so a span ending at\n    24:00 joins one starting at 00:00 the next day, and returns the merged\n    *half-open range* values to the caller.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:shared.sigil:941",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:shared.sigil:SharedKernel",
      "componentLabel": "SharedKernel",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "shared.sigil",
      "prose": "    The time and domain-error rules of SharedKernel must not import database access\n    or framework code, so every rule on a local span or UTC instant stays a pure\n    function.\n"
    }
  ],
